WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.169
WIL WILLIS: Joshua,
Jesse, congratulations.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.537
You guys have landed
in the final round

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.571
of this competition.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.073
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.709
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:14.014
That weapon is a Lochaber ax.

00:00:16.548 --> 00:00:17.216
Good luck.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.817
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:19.618
 Good luck.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:20.420
 Good luck.

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.359
We're back at my home
forge in Liverpool,

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:29.295
and I'm ready to get
started on the Lochaber ax.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.331
Finishing something that's
this big that I've never

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.800
done before in such a
short amount of time

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.534
is a huge challenge.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.970
Forging everything by
hand has its advantages

00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:38.971
and disadvantages.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.139
The advantage is
that you learn how

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:42.007
to move steel pretty quickly.

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:43.642
But the disadvantage
is that it takes

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.244
its toll on you physically.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:49.549
I'll be forced to
width today, and I'll

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.583
be forced to length today.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.885 line:0%
I'm going to make the
best blade I can make,

00:00:52.951 --> 00:00:59.158 line:7%
and hopefully it's a $10,000 ax.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.860
 I have four days
instead of the five days,

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:04.530
so that means there's no time
to waste in this contest.

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:07.099
There's five pieces
to this entire build,

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:11.203
so getting everything to
mesh together perfectly,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.073
that's going to be
the biggest challenge.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.209
I know that when we
get to the testing

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.979
that I have to make sure that
this thing is as sturdy and as

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.347
stout as possible,
because they are

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:24.650
going to beat the ever-loving
crap out of this thing.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.120
This is a war machine,
so I want to make sure

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.422
that it is a lightweight blade.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.723
If the blade is
too heavy, I mean,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.958
that could be the
difference between winning

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.694
and losing this competition.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.900
JOSHUA: Today I'm going
to profile the blade

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.102
and get the bevel on it.

00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:45.405
I also want to get
that hook attached

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:49.141
today, too, so it's
going to be a busy day.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.810
I forged out my hook.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:55.948
And as I'm grinding the hook,
there's a crack in my hook,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.450
right down the middle.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:01.087
I don't want to fucking have to
start goddamn shit over again.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.656
I can't afford to
lose any time today.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.058
And I need to do this again.

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:08.494
Ugh, I don't have time
to do things twice.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.295
I'm running a
little behind today,

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:12.798
so I don't have time to
fuck with it too much.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:15.468 line:7%
I got to kick it up a notch.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.238 line:0%
JESSE: Day four, I got a lot
of handwork that I have to do.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:22.074
There's a lot of hand sanding,
polishing, ruling, so a lot

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:24.243
of small tedious work today.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.112
Eight and a half pounds.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:29.182
I'm about two and a
half pounds over what I

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:31.150
actually wanted to have there.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.918
It's little bit more
difficult to swing

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.254
and everything like that.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.488
And there's a couple of little
tabs that I can cut off.

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.791
The nuts, and the bolts, and
everything like that, that's

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.961
coming out for rivets.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.797
I shaved off a
good pound, and it

00:02:44.863 --> 00:02:46.232
definitely feels much lighter.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.634
I hope that the weight
isn't the determining factor

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.736
when it comes down to
the final judgment.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.739
This challenge was
absolutely a wrecking ball,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.175
but I love this blade.

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.078
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, bladesmiths.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.747
This is the kill test.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.681
Now, to find out how
lethal your weapons are,

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.684
I will take your Lochabers
and deliver killing

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.987
blows on this pig carcass.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:08.821
Joshua, you're up first.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:09.689
You ready for this?

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:10.756
 Yeah, let's do it.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.225
I don't mind going first,
other than the fact

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.095
that I might pass out
because of anticipation.

00:03:16.161 --> 00:03:18.431
But I'm ready to see
this thing get to work.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.840
[rock music]

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:34.814
[blow impacts]

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.600
DOUG MARCAIDA:
All right, Joshua.

00:03:54.666 --> 00:03:58.571
First up, your blade,
it's a pork chopper.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.173
On its thrust, did you
see the wound channel?

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.977
It creates such
a big, deep gash.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.744
It's fun to wield.

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:06.646
It's sharp.

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:09.248
And most importantly,
it will kill.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:09.982
Good job.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:10.983
 Thank you.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.084
 All right, Jesse.
Your turn.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:12.885
Are you ready?

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:13.653
 Absolutely.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.553
Let's do it.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.055
I'm really anxious
about this test.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.490
It's a little bit heavy.

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:18.724
I'm hoping that that's not going
to be a determining factor.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.460
I don't know how
this is going to go.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.767
[rock music]

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:33.740
[blow impacts]

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.462
 First up, your
blade has the weight

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.398
that every chop into
something, want to keep going.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.368
It wants to keep going, and
going, and going to where

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.737
it pretty much took me with it.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.239
Good chops, good cuts.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:09.808
And more importantly,
it will kill.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:10.676
 Thank you.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:11.376
 All right.

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:13.245
Up next, the strength test.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:14.780
Dave.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:17.216
 To test the strength
and overall construction

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.051
of your weapons, I'll
be hooking the shield,

00:05:19.084 --> 00:05:22.321
pulling it into place, and then
attacking it with the blade.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.689
All right, Josh,
you're up first.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:24.223
Are you ready?

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.124
 Oh yeah.

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:27.727
[rock music]

00:05:32.731 --> 00:05:37.603
[blow impacts]

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:54.053
 So first off, you took a
little bit of deformation

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:57.757
here, pretty much where that
edge caught some of the studs

00:05:57.824 --> 00:05:59.057
on that shield.

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:01.427
But it's still sharp.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:04.096
It's really a nicely built
piece, got a good look to it.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.065
It's easy to wield.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:08.000
Everything's still solid.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:09.568
Strong ax-- nicely done.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.970
- Thank you.
- All right, Jesse.

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:11.737
Your turn.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:12.304
Are you ready?

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:13.740
 Absolutely.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:24.350
[rock music]

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:28.588
[blow impacts]

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:38.998
 All right, Jesse.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:42.168
You can see on your
blade here where you've

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:44.303
taken a pretty good roll here.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.872
And this is sort of
a roll and a chip.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:51.743
But everywhere else on
this blade is still sharp.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:52.678
Nicely done.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:53.579
 Thank you.

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:54.613
DAVID BAKER: All
right, gentlemen.

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:56.215
Next up, the sharpness test.

00:06:56.281 --> 00:06:57.683
And for that, I'll
give you to Doug.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.624
 This is the sugar-cane slice.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.492
Now, to find out how
sharp your weapons are,

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:08.494
I will take your
weapons and deliver cuts

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.663
across these sugar-cane bundles.

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:12.231
Joshua, you're up first.
Ready for this?

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:13.633
- Let's do it, man.
- Let's do it.

00:07:22.374 --> 00:07:24.877
[suspenseful music]

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:29.849
[blow impacts]

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.593
DOUG MARCAIDA:
All right, Joshua.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:44.230
You contoured this shaft here
so that when you hold onto it,

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:46.232
you can really tell
where the edge is.

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:47.799
I really like that.

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:50.403
Overall, sir, your
weapon is sharp.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:53.071
It cuts all the way
through cleanly.

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:54.106
It will cut.

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:55.074
 Thank you.

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:56.041
 All right, Jesse.
Your turn.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:56.842
Are you ready?

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.010
 You betcha.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:00.679
It feels like I might be
kind of at a setback right

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:03.749
now just because my edge seemed
like it took more damage.

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:05.751 line:0%
It can come down to
the finest details.

00:08:09.154 --> 00:08:11.557
[suspenseful music]

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:14.292
[blow impacts]

00:08:14.359 --> 00:08:15.094
 Nice.

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:28.173
 All right, Jesse.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.742
The blade is heavy.

00:08:29.808 --> 00:08:32.578
It cuts, but also you can
feel the weight behind it

00:08:32.611 --> 00:08:34.313
crush the rest of it.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.283
Overall, sir, for this
test, it will cut.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:39.452
 Thank you.

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:40.553
JOSHUA: Who's going
to win this challenge?

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.486
I have no idea.

00:08:41.553 --> 00:08:43.022
We are neck and neck.

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:45.791
It's really anybody's game
right now it's a toss-up.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:49.995
 Josh, Jesse, both
of you guys brought

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:53.866
in finale weapons that performed
incredibly well in our tests.

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:56.635
Only one of you can be the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:56.702 --> 00:09:01.974
And that champion is Josh.

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:02.908
Congratulations.

00:09:02.974 --> 00:09:04.310
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:07.880
Jesse, unfortunately your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:09:07.946 --> 00:09:10.015
 Jesse, you brought
us a fantastic weapon.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:12.318
And this came down to
the finest of details.

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:13.919
Your weapon took
a bit more damage,

00:09:13.985 --> 00:09:15.521
and your opponent's
weapon was a little bit

00:09:15.587 --> 00:09:16.988
lighter and easier to control.

00:09:17.055 --> 00:09:19.091
For those reasons,
we're letting you go.

00:09:19.124 --> 00:09:19.959
 All right.

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:23.629
 Jesse, please,
surrender your weapon.

00:09:23.662 --> 00:09:24.930
JESSE: Second place is--

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:27.866
it's not fun, but Josh
brought a better blade.

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:31.036
I give it my best, and I
put my best work out there.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:34.072
I came here to prove to
myself that I'm not just

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:37.276
a backyard knife maker,
and I'm ecstatic that I

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:38.110
made it this far.

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:42.381
 All right, Josh.

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:43.449
Congratulations.

00:09:43.515 --> 00:09:44.916
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:47.987
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:48.988
Good job, brother.

00:09:49.055 --> 00:09:50.155
 Yeah, it's amazing.

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:51.190
It's an amazing feeling.

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:54.493
 Please present your
blade to the judges.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.861
[laughing]

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:57.396
What?

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:59.364
Are you kidding?

00:09:59.431 --> 00:10:00.666
Holy crap.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:03.435
I'm the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:07.006
I'm-- I'm speechless.

